ZERO TOOLS 0.16 PREVIEW - 25 NOVEMBER 2026

Two additions from the accessible idea catalogue 1-1000 are now implemented
in original Zero for native Linux x86-64 and Windows x64. Idea 723 adds the
read-only zero-inspect header card for five own formats. It reads at most
4096 bytes, validates header consistency and declared lengths, and reports
that payload structure and integrity remain unchecked. It never executes
or extracts input. See tools/inspect.ztext.

Idea 898 adds zero-web --help and --capabilities without opening a document
or graphical display, and zero-web --about as a built-in graphical page
through the existing DOM/CSS/raster pipeline. The original diagnostic page
browser/engine/capabilities-demo.ztext exercises CSS cascade, display:none,
BR line breaks and JavaScript textContent. See browser/engine/CAPABILITIES.ztext.

The build now has 82 stages and 78 outputs. A second build with its freshly
built own builder reproduced every artifact byte for byte. All 68 previous
artifacts other than the builder/browser pairs are unchanged, including
both kernels, all boot components, ISO, guest apps and compilers. No new
boot behavior or physical hardware validation is claimed by this update.

The inspector parser passed 13757 original Zero checks on Linux and Windows
under Wine. New browser CLI checks passed 34 Linux/35 Wine scenarios. GUI about
page scrolling, Home and Escape passed on Linux/Xvfb and Windows/Wine, with
five exact cross-platform pixel matches. The engine integration 35 checks
passed in the final build. Module docs give the remaining test details.

These are native tool additions, not guest kernel integration. The native
browser still has no HTTP/HTTPS fetching, TLS or full web compatibility.
Source IDEAS.ztext identifies the real catalogue and limits: the newer
1155-4154 lists were received only by title and are not claimed implemented.
No background task or new hourly automation was created.

Existing user data disks are unchanged. Raw SHA256:
