Prior work records follow chronologically; this section describes 0.16.

Zero OS 0.13 verification - 2026-11-18

Product implementation is original Zero; documentation uses own ZTEXT001.
Tests check behavior, boundaries and preservation, not merely file extensions.
External emulator firmware and test orchestration are outside the project.

Compiler and native targets
Own application stages reproduce identical bytes.182 main compiler checks
passed;47 capacity/host-interface checks passed on Linux and Windows/Wine.
Actual IA32 VM checks exercised fullu64 arithmetic, all64local slots including
short-displacement boundaries16/17, literal127/128 and128two-worker rounds.
The new native GUI interfaces were checked for Linux syscall arguments,
Windows12-argument calls, stack alignment and target restrictions.

Browser components
100 original Zero HTTP parser checks passed: framing, Content-Length,
chunked extensions/trailers, MIME/status/Location, ambiguous lengths,
malformed/oversized data and unsupported compression.
170 HTML reader checks passed:70 semantic/boundary cases and100 deterministic
malformed probes. All ran on Linux, Windows/Wine and in an actualIA32 VM.
Wrapped output/title pointers are rejected without error-cleanup dereference.
76 original Zero navigation/UI/frame checks passed: URL normalization,
unsafe schemes, query/fragments, redirects, history rollover/back/reload,
keyboard limits, buffer canaries and unchanged URL/link inputs. Page bytes
never entered the shell command buffer in these checks.

Browser VM matrix
The first fullBIOS64 candidate passed68checks, including negative network
responses, plain/HTML/Unicode, links/history, chunked and23KiBpages, script
suppression, redirects, HTTPS refusal, PS/2input, real diskfiles andcoldboot.
The subsequent candidate passed140checks acrossBIOS64(36),BIOS32(32),
UEFI64(36),UEFI32(36), adding normalizedrelative/query/fragment paths.
Optional serial-test socket backpressure was diagnosed using a continuously
drained FIFO; GUI and mouse remained active. A real idle pointer flicker was
then found and fixed by preserving the overlay until a repaint is needed.
The fix checks all visible window rings and restores requested pixel writes
under the pointer;11 extra native dirty/visibility/overlay cases passed.

Editors
Guest core:28 event/render and7actual file-service coroutine cases passed.
BIOS64 andBIOS32 each passed20memory/state assertions plus12terminal file
checks, including4checks aftercoldboot. Zero andEzero compile/run, save/open,
400-byte bounds, dirty-discard guards and preservation were tested.
UEFI64 andUEFI32 each executedboth languages and8terminal checks including
saved-file persistence aftercoldboot. These are separate from browser counts.

Native Studio used real Linux/Xorg and Windows/Wine windows. For bothlanguages,
tests typed sources, saved, compiled inprocess, executed outputs, rebuilt
deterministically, moved the caret with mouse/keys, reopenedfiles, rejected
missing/invalidinputs, protectedunsavedchanges and preservedpreviousbinaries
aftercompileerrors. An independent originalZero file harness passed10cases:
missing/binary/oversized/symlink inputs, CRLFbuffer-normalization, normal/empty
save, existingtempfile, failedrename and500-bytepathboundaries.
Relocated native kits are separately extracted and checked before publication.

Scope and evidence
Windows execution evidence uses Wine, not a physical Windows installation.
Boot evidence uses QEMU BIOS/OVMF; no new VirtualBox or realhardware result
is claimed. The nativeLinux editor requires X11/Xwayland; nativeASCII limit
65535bytes, guestASCII limit400bytes. One document, keyboard guest UI, noIDE
debugger. Browser lacksTLS/CSS/JavaScript/DOM/forms/media and cannot support
all sites. No tested result establishes absence of every possible bug.

